# Deploy-only ignore. Heavy non-build assets the Next.js build never reads.
#
# `docs/*` not `docs`, with one exception re-included below. Excluding the
# DIRECTORY makes it impossible to re-include anything inside it, which is a
# gitignore rule Vercel inherits, and that is what broke every deployment from
# this branch: `scripts/check-pricing-lock.mjs` runs in prebuild and parses
# docs/PRICING.md as the authority for every fee figure, so with the whole
# directory excluded the guard reported "docs/PRICING.md is missing" and blocked
# the build every single time. A guard that can never pass is not a lock, it is
# a wall, and it fails identically whether the pricing is right or wrong.
#
# Anything a BUILD-TIME guard reads must be listed here as an exception.
#
# It happened a SECOND time on 2026-08-12, the same way, and the line above is
# the reason it was quick to diagnose. `payment-critical-doctrine.mjs` was
# registered as a build guard and reads docs/security/CREDENTIAL-ROTATION.md to
# check clause (d), that every payment-critical variable has a recorded rotation
# procedure. Locally it passed. On Vercel the file was not there, so it reported
# all TEN variables as having no rotation row and blocked the deploy. The guard
# was right about what it could see and wrong about the world.
#
# The lesson is already written in docs/roast/FALSE-POSITIVE-CHECKLIST.md entry
# 5: a guard that reads anything outside the source tree must be drilled in
# EVERY environment it runs in, and a production build host is the one most
# likely to differ. Local green is not evidence for Vercel.
#
# AND THE RE-INCLUSION HAS TO WALK THE DIRECTORY DOWN. `!docs/security/CREDENTIAL-
# ROTATION.md` on its own does NOTHING, which cost a second failed deploy to see:
# `docs/*` excludes the `docs/security` DIRECTORY, and the gitignore rule at the
# top of this file applies at every level, so a file inside an excluded directory
# can never be re-included. docs/PRICING.md works only because it sits directly
# under docs/ and is therefore excluded as a FILE.
#
# So each level is re-included, then re-excluded, then the one file is named.
docs/*
!docs/PRICING.md
!docs/security/
docs/security/*
!docs/security/CREDENTIAL-ROTATION.md
design-captures
research
audit-v2
.git
